---
import Demo from '../../layouts/Demo.astro';
---

<Demo slug="sketch-entropy">
  <div class="stage panel" data-stage>
    <p class="stage__loading" data-status>Loading the WebAssembly module…</p>

    <div class="stage__body" data-body hidden>
      <section class="block">
        <h2>The two folds</h2>
        <div class="folds">
          <article class="fold fold--bad">
            <p class="label">Retracted</p>
            <h3>naive</h3>
            <pre><code>sketch ^= seeds[b] + W</code></pre>
            <p class="fold__why">
              The window is only 0 to 63. Adding it straight to a seed perturbs the low bits and
              leaves the upper 56 a function of bit counts alone. A nominal 64-bit sketch takes at
              most <strong class="num">256</strong> distinct values.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="fold fold--good">
            <p class="label">In use</p>
            <h3>fixed</h3>
            <pre><code>sketch ^= seeds[b] +
         W * 0x9E3779B97F4A7C15</code></pre>
            <p class="fold__why">
              Multiplying by an odd constant first spreads all 64 window values across the full
              word, so every bit position carries window-dependent entropy.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="block">
        <h2>Run both over the same random streams</h2>
        <p class="prose">
          Each stream gets a fixed length between 1 and 400 bits, drawn uniformly. Both folds are
          applied to the identical stream sequence, so the only difference is the arithmetic. The
          work happens in Go inside the WebAssembly module, chunked so the page stays responsive —
          the progress bar is real.
        </p>

        <div class="controls">
          <label class="field field--narrow">
            <span class="label">Streams</span>
            <input type="number" data-streams min="1000" max="200000" step="1000" value="20000" />
          </label>
          <label class="field field--narrow">
            <span class="label">Seed</span>
            <input type="number" data-seed value="1" />
          </label>
          <button type="button" data-run class="btn btn--primary">Run both</button>
        </div>

        <div class="bars" data-bars>
          <p class="bars__idle">Nothing run yet.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="block">
        <h2>The case the fix does not address</h2>
        <p class="prose">
          A working all-zero stream is the pathological case. The window stays at zero, so the fold
          degenerates to a parity count and yields only <strong class="num">2</strong> distinct
          sketches at every length. The odd multiplier cannot help, because there is no window to
          spread. This is documented rather than fixed.
        </p>
        <p class="prose caveat">
          And there is still no collision guarantee. About <strong>1.5%</strong> of random streams
          of length 1 to 200 collide, with the first collision near stream 350. The sketch is a
          state fingerprint for divergence tracking, not a stable identifier.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="block">
        <h2>Where the bug had already spread</h2>
        <p class="prose">
          The core fold was fixed and covered by
          <code>TestSketchEntropy</code>. But two structural-calibration paths inlined the old form
          and were never covered, so the collapsed sketch survived in the repository for as long as
          it did. <code>fsvm.SketchTerm</code>'s doc comment said every hand-rolled ingest path
          must use it — and a comment did not stop it happening twice. The fix was two call sites
          plus assertions that check each one independently.
        </p>
        <pre class="wide"><code>internal/transponder/structural.go:64   s.Sketch ^= s.Seeds[b] + uint64(s.W)   // was
internal/transponder/threshold.go:116  s.Sketch ^= s.Seeds[b] + uint64(s.W)   // was

// now, in both places:
s.Sketch ^= fsvm.SketchTerm(s.Seeds, b, s.W)</code></pre>
        <p class="prose">
          Reverting either fix makes the regression test fail: distinct sketches drop from about
          1,982 per 2,000 streams to <strong class="num">255</strong>. That is the only way a
          finding like this stays fixed — not a comment, not a convention, an assertion.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</Demo>

<script>
  import { invoke } from '../../lib/fib';
  import { need, nextFrame, setStatus } from '../../lib/ui';

  interface EntropyOut {
    variant: string;
    /** Cumulative across the session, so it is safe to display directly. */
    distinct: number;
    total: number;
    collisions: number;
    chunkDistinct: number;
    chunkTotal: number;
    firstCollisionInChunk: number;
    cap: number;
    meanPopcount: number;
    seed: number;
    minLen: number;
    maxLen: number;
    done: boolean;
    offset: number;
    session: string;
  }

  const status = need<HTMLElement>('[data-status]');
  const body = need<HTMLElement>('[data-body]');
  const streamsInput = need<HTMLInputElement>('[data-streams]');
  const seedInput = need<HTMLInputElement>('[data-seed]');
  const runBtn = need<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-run]');
  const barsBox = need<HTMLElement>('[data-bars]');

  interface Acc {
    distinct: number;
    total: number;
    collisions: number;
    firstCollision: number;
    pop: number | null;
    done: boolean;
  }

  function blank(): Acc {
    return { distinct: 0, total: 0, collisions: 0, firstCollision: 0, pop: null, done: false };
  }

  /**
   * Sweep a variant in chunks.
   *
   * Two things make this correct rather than merely plausible.
   *
   * Chunking: Go/WASM runs synchronously on the browser's event loop, so one
   * 20,000-stream call is ~8 million steps and would freeze the tab for a
   * second. Chunk size is 2,000 and we yield between calls, so the progress bar
   * actually moves.
   *
   * Session: `distinct` is only meaningful as a union across the whole sweep.
   * Passing a session id makes the Go side carry the seen-set between calls and
   * return a cumulative count. Without it, each chunk reports its own distinct
   * total, and adding those up over-counts badly — the naive fold saturates at
   * 256 per chunk, so three chunks would claim 768 distinct values for a fold
   * that mathematically cannot exceed 256.
   */
  async function sweep(
    variant: string,
    streams: number,
    seed: number,
    session: string,
  ): Promise<Acc> {
    const acc = blank();
    const CHUNK = 2000;
    let offset = 0;
    while (offset < streams) {
      const { data } = await invoke<EntropyOut>('sketch.entropy', {
        variant,
        streams,
        seed,
        offset,
        count: CHUNK,
        minLen: 1,
        maxLen: 400,
        session,
        reset: offset === 0,
      });
      acc.distinct = data.distinct;
      acc.total = data.total;
      acc.collisions = data.collisions;
      acc.firstCollision = data.firstCollisionInChunk || acc.firstCollision;
      acc.pop = data.meanPopcount;
      acc.done = data.done;
      offset += data.chunkTotal;
      render(variant, acc, streams);
      await nextFrame();
    }
    return acc;
  }

  function render(variant: string, acc: Acc, target: number): void {
    const card = barsBox.querySelector<HTMLElement>(`[data-card="${variant}"]`);
    if (!card) return;
    const pct = target ? (acc.total / target) * 100 : 0;

    const distinctEl = card.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-field="distinct"]')!;
    const collisionsEl = card.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-field="collisions"]')!;
    const popEl = card.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-field="pop"]')!;
    const firstEl = card.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-field="first"]')!;
    const fillEl = card.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-fill]')!;
    const pctEl = card.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-pct]')!;

    distinctEl.textContent = acc.distinct.toLocaleString('en-US');
    collisionsEl.textContent = acc.collisions.toLocaleString('en-US');
    popEl.textContent = acc.pop != null ? acc.pop.toFixed(1) : '—';
    firstEl.textContent = acc.firstCollision ? acc.firstCollision.toLocaleString('en-US') : 'none yet';
    fillEl.style.width = `${Math.min(pct, 100).toFixed(1)}%`;
    pctEl.textContent = `${acc.total.toLocaleString('en-US')} / ${target.toLocaleString('en-US')}`;

    // Distinctness as a share of the sample, which is the number that makes
    // "256" legible next to "19,713".
    const rate = acc.total ? (acc.distinct / acc.total) * 100 : 0;
    card.dataset.rate = rate.toFixed(1);
    card.dataset.done = String(acc.done);
  }

  function buildCards(variants: Array<{ key: string; label: string; cap: number; note: string }>): void {
    barsBox.replaceChildren(
      ...variants.map((v) => {
        const card = document.createElement('div');
        card.className = 'bar-card';
        card.dataset.card = v.key;
        card.dataset.kind = v.key;

        const head = document.createElement('div');
        head.className = 'bar-card__head';
        const h = document.createElement('h3');
        h.textContent = v.label;
        const pct = document.createElement('span');
        pct.className = 'bar-card__pct num';
        pct.dataset.pct = '';
        pct.textContent = 'not started';
        head.append(h, pct);

        const track = document.createElement('div');
        track.className = 'bar-card__track';
        const fill = document.createElement('div');
        fill.className = 'bar-card__fill';
        fill.dataset.fill = '';
        fill.style.width = '0%';
        track.append(fill);

        const dl = document.createElement('dl');
        dl.className = 'bar-card__stats';
        const rows: Array<[string, string]> = [
          ['distinct sketches', 'distinct'],
          ['collisions', 'collisions'],
          ['mean popcount', 'pop'],
          ['first collision', 'first'],
        ];
        for (const [label, field] of rows) {
          const dt = document.createElement('dt');
          dt.textContent = label;
          const dd = document.createElement('dd');
          dd.className = 'num';
          dd.dataset.field = field;
          dd.textContent = '—';
          dl.append(dt, dd);
        }

        const cap = document.createElement('p');
        cap.className = 'bar-card__cap';
        cap.textContent = v.note;

        card.append(head, track, dl, cap);
        return card;
      }),
    );
  }

  async function boot(): Promise<void> {
    try {
      await invoke('fsvm.meta', {});
      body.hidden = false;
      status.hidden = true;
      buildCards([
        {
          key: 'naive',
          label: 'naive · seeds[b] + W',
          cap: 256,
          note: 'Theoretical ceiling 256 distinct values, from 2 seeds × 64 window values. It cannot do better than that however many streams you feed it.',
        },
        {
          key: 'fixed',
          label: 'fixed · seeds[b] + W × odd',
          cap: 0,
          note: 'No structural ceiling. Distinctness tracks the sample size, which is the entire point of the fix.',
        },
      ]);
    } catch (err) {
      setStatus(status, (err as Error).message, 'error');
    }
  }

  runBtn.addEventListener('click', async () => {
    runBtn.disabled = true;
    runBtn.textContent = 'Running…';
    const streams = Math.max(Number(streamsInput.value) || 20000, 100);
    const seed = Number(seedInput.value) || 1;
    try {
      buildCards([
        {
          key: 'naive',
          label: 'naive · seeds[b] + W',
          cap: 256,
          note: 'Theoretical ceiling 256 distinct values, from 2 seeds × 64 window values. It cannot do better than that however many streams you feed it.',
        },
        {
          key: 'fixed',
          label: 'fixed · seeds[b] + W × odd',
          cap: 0,
          note: 'No structural ceiling. Distinctness tracks the sample size, which is the entire point of the fix.',
        },
      ]);
      // Sequential, not parallel: both sweeps hammer the same event loop.
      await sweep('naive', streams, seed, 'naive-sweep');
      await sweep('fixed', streams, seed, 'fixed-sweep');
      // Hand the accumulated seen-sets back so a long-lived tab does not carry
      // them for the rest of the session.
      try {
        await invoke('sketch.sessions.reset', {});
      } catch {
        // Non-fatal: the maps are bounded and a later sweep resets its own.
      }
    } catch (err) {
      setStatus(status, (err as Error).message, 'error');
    } finally {
      runBtn.disabled = false;
      runBtn.textContent = 'Run both';
    }
  });

  void boot();
</script>

<style>
  .stage {
    padding: 1.6rem 1.75rem 1.75rem;
  }
  .stage__loading {
    color: var(--ink-dim);
    padding: 2rem 0;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .stage__loading[data-kind='error'] {
    color: var(--retract-lit);
    text-align: left;
    white-space: pre-wrap;
  }

  .block + .block {
    margin-top: 2.75rem;
    padding-top: 2.25rem;
    border-top: var(--rule-w) solid var(--rule);
  }
  h2 {
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  h3 {
    font-size: 1rem;
  }

  .prose {
    color: var(--ink-dim);
    font-size: 0.93rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    max-width: var(--measure);
    margin-bottom: 1.1rem;
  }
  .prose.caveat {
    padding: 1rem 1.2rem;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--retract);
    background: var(--retract-wash);
    border-radius: 0 var(--radius-sm) var(--radius-sm) 0;
  }

  pre.wide {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin: 1rem 0;
    overflow-x: auto;
  }

  /* ---- Folds ---- */
  .folds {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.15rem;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 20rem), 1fr));
  }
  .fold {
    padding: 1.25rem 1.4rem;
    background: var(--surface);
    border: var(--rule-w) solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  }
  .fold--bad {
    border-left: 3px solid var(--retract);
  }
  .fold--good {
    border-left: 3px solid var(--verify);
  }
  .fold h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    margin: 0.4rem 0 0.75rem;
  }
  .fold pre {
    font-size: 0.76rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.85rem;
  }
  .fold__why {
    font-size: 0.86rem;
    color: var(--ink-dim);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  /* ---- Controls ---- */
  .controls {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 1rem;
    align-items: flex-end;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }
  .field {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.35rem;
  }
  .field--narrow {
    flex: 0 0 9rem;
  }
  .btn--primary {
    color: var(--brass-lit);
    border-color: var(--brass-dim);
  }

  /* ---- Result cards ---- */
  .bars__idle {
    color: var(--ink-mute);
    font-size: 0.88rem;
  }
  .bars {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.25rem;
  }
  .bar-card {
    background: var(--surface-sunk);
    border: var(--rule-w) solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    box-shadow: var(--sunk-sm);
    padding: 1.2rem 1.35rem;
  }
  .bar-card[data-kind='naive'] {
    border-color: color-mix(in oklab, var(--retract) 45%, var(--rule));
  }
  .bar-card[data-kind='fixed'] {
    border-color: color-mix(in oklab, var(--verify) 45%, var(--rule));
  }

  .bar-card__head {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  .bar-card__head h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
  }
  .bar-card__pct {
    font-size: 0.76rem;
    color: var(--ink-mute);
  }

  .bar-card__track {
    height: 10px;
    margin: 0.85rem 0 1rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--surface);
    box-shadow: var(--sunk-sm);
    border: var(--rule-w) solid var(--rule);
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .bar-card__fill {
    height: 100%;
    width: 0;
    border-radius: 999px;
    transition: width 0.18s var(--ease);
  }
  [data-kind='naive'] .bar-card__fill {
    background: var(--retract);
  }
  [data-kind='fixed'] .bar-card__fill {
    background: var(--verify);
  }

  .bar-card__stats {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 9rem), 1fr));
    gap: 0.75rem 1.25rem;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .bar-card__stats dt {
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-mute);
    margin-bottom: 0.15rem;
  }
  .bar-card__stats dd {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  [data-kind='naive'] .bar-card__stats dd {
    color: var(--retract-lit);
  }
  [data-kind='fixed'] .bar-card__stats dd {
    color: var(--verify-lit);
  }

  .bar-card__cap {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    font-size: 0.79rem;
    color: var(--ink-mute);
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .bar-card__fill {
      transition: none;
    }
  }
</style>
